ments and regulatory changes to the Firearms Act and the Authorization to Carry (ATC) Regulations to protect Jewish institutions.; Approach to foreign governments and their commitments regarding education, including ensuring that Canadian funds are not used to develop resources that promote hate or indoctrination, as well as governance and accountability.; That the Government of Canada formally recognize the national crisis of antisemitism and establish a federal task force to develop a coordinated, nationwide response.; Ensure that digital gaming platforms are regulated as online services under Bill C-34, An Act to enact the Digital Safety Act and the Digital Safety Commission of Canada Act and to make consequential amendments to other Acts; Expedite three Private Members’ Bills in the 45th Parliament that would help strengthen protections for religious minorities across Canada, including the Jewish community: Bill C-255, An Act to amend 
